{"title":"1989 USAMO Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/8/a98921ac8588f67c4d2279bba0fddeecb3107fe3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(z)= z^n + c_1 z^{n-1} + c_2 z^{n-2} + \\cdots + c_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"310\" height=\"21\" /> be a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Polynomial\" title=\"Polynomial\">polynomial</a> in the complex variable <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, with real coefficients <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/d/3bd87559f4e4c9af40246a0fdbafe6feab507414.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" />. Suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/8/4782f9100cc011f1d97a4dfc0517ad836176e58d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|P(i)| &lt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"18\" />. Prove that there exist real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/6/f36c82a9b9fe5c485dbd9230b0440c5578749ed7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(a + bi) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"107\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/7/d073646141e953c1b3d4049346c2a792e53c2c8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a^2 + b^2 + 1)^2 &lt; 4 b^2 + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"186\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/b/12bbab6df649a8426d1dbb7af4021eba8e02702a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_1, \\dotsc, z_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"73\" height=\"11\" /> be the (not necessarily distinct) roots of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, so that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/a/a1a69d793f02478695c7e30890e6c2d1997dc0d2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[P(z) = \\prod_{j=1}^n (z- z_j) .\\]\" width=\"149\" height=\"50\" />\nSince all the coefficients of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are real, it follows that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/e/9ee4b825a2e36ae093ed7be5e4851ef453b34914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> is a root of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/e/74eb05c3053d67982f254adc11fc9e4cd945cad3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P( \\overline{w}) = \\overline{ P(w)} = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"140\" height=\"21\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/0/db05290107b3775c5bb91d94060a1e60461a1771.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{w}$\" width=\"14\" height=\"11\" />, the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Complex_conjugate\" title=\"Complex conjugate\">complex conjugate</a> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/e/9ee4b825a2e36ae093ed7be5e4851ef453b34914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" />, is also a root of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Since\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/09480c612c9efe4ec98ce55e0cbf263c946c58a8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\lvert i- z_1 \\rvert \\cdot \\lvert i - z_2 \\rvert  \\dotsm \\lvert i - z_n \\rvert = \\lvert P(i) \\rvert &lt; 1,\\]\" width=\"309\" height=\"18\" />\nit follows that for some (not necessarily distinct) conjugates <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/3/7532b41a34c9ca592694135d1de65eeb8d9ce036.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/2/762a43137e1d61e8a958446459e86ac7ed0022d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" />,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/7/b8746c4ae01ad722930248ea94ec62e04927b0f1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\lvert z_i-i \\rvert \\cdot \\lvert z_j-i \\rvert &lt; 1.\\]\" width=\"154\" height=\"19\" />\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/7/11740b597418df7b1a768d236c62d87d62622456.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_i = a+bi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"83\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/b/16be3203403df52651e4772958358ee454929a05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_j = a-bi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"85\" height=\"17\" />, for real <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/b/e9bdf3e496517e8f8742f81dd774be1f93cf6e8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"18\" />.  We note that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/0/390afbd17dcbcddb01897c0211dc198b865891bb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(a+b+1)^2 - (a+b-1)^2 = 4a + 4b .\\]\" width=\"291\" height=\"19\" />\nThus\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/d/a6d61aa24ecd79f5cc753fe4ece0cce01209658f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} (a^2+b^2+1)^2 &amp;= (a^2+b^2-1)^2 + 4a^2 + 4b^2 = \\lvert a^2 + b^2 - 1 - 2ai \\rvert ^2 + 4b^2 \\\\ &amp;= \\lvert (a-i)^2 - (bi)^2 \\rvert^2 + 4b^2 \\\\ &amp;= \\bigl( \\lvert a+bi - i \\rvert \\cdot \\lvert a-bi -i \\rvert \\bigr)^2 + 4b^2 \\\\ &amp;= \\bigl( \\lvert z_i - i \\rvert \\cdot \\lvert z_j - i \\rvert \\bigr)^2 + 4b^2 &lt; 1+4b^2. \\end{align*}\" width=\"552\" height=\"112\" />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/a/a4aa162ae2164f71614eb5181904464aaf26f413.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(a+bi) = P(z_i) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"176\" height=\"20\" />, these real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/b/e9bdf3e496517e8f8742f81dd774be1f93cf6e8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"18\" /> satisfy the problem's conditions.  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_USAMO\" title=\"1989 USAMO\">1989 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"1989 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=1989\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1989 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1989 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1989 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1989 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1989 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1989 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/viewtopic.php?p=356637#356637\">Discussion on AoPS/MathLinks</a></li></ul>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017082750\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.029 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.053 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 194/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1267/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5808/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   15.675      1 -total\n 66.26%   10.386      1 Template:USAMO_box\n 32.35%    5.071      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:5471:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017082750 and revision id 79449. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}